WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.036
 Bladesmiths, congratulations.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.403
You've made it to the final
round of this competition.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.038
Now it's time to send
you back to your home

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:09.409
forges to recreate this
iconic weapon from history--

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.247
the boar sword.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.047
Good luck.

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:16.849
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.018
 Good job, man.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.356
JONATHAN: So it's day one.

00:00:24.456 --> 00:00:26.559
Excited to get to work
on this boar sword.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.061 line:7%
Ready to knock it out.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.797
I've never made
anything this big.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.364
It's going to be an
interesting build.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:36.536
Swinging this four-pound sledge
is getting heavy already.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:40.106
My game plan for today
is to get at least half

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.174
of the sword force out.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.176
I want to get those
curves established.

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:47.179
It's definitely interesting
hammering those waves in there,

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:50.416
because the blade will
want to walk sideways.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.953 line:0%
And so having to bring it back
to establish that edge to edge

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.689 line:0%
straightness, it's
difficult. I was hoping

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.459 line:0%
to be able to get a little bit
farther along than what I did,

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:03.863 line:0%
but I think it's
going pretty well.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.098 line:0%
 Bit of a geometry
dilemma here,

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.635 line:0%
and I'm hitting the
ceiling before I can

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.404 line:7%
hit the blade on the grinder.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.106
So I'm going to have to either
take some extra whet out

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.175
here, make a cutout here.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.344
I can't underestimate
the size of this blade.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.580
I got to be really careful
while I'm trying to grind

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.881
it in my tiny little shop.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.549
Perfect.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.985
So after cutting away
a bit of the table

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:29.889
and a bit of the roof, it
seems to be working now.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.158
So I just finished
forging up the crossbar,

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.826
so it's time to quench.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.062
If this goes well, I'll be set
up really well for the rest

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.096
of this competition.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.132
If it goes poorly, the opposite.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.701
This crossbar is
making it a lot more

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.102
difficult than I
was anticipating

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:44.470
to get this whole blade hot.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.639
Fortunately, it
should be OK still.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:48.508
Here we go.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.045
[blowing]

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.247
[blade scraping]

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.547
That's the sound
I wanted to hear.

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.584 line:7%
Ha ha.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.720
JONATHAN: Today, I hope to
accomplish the heat treat.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.656
This is the biggest thing
I've ever heat treated.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:07.627
I've got a forge that I'm
borrowing from a buddy of mine.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.295
It's a five-burner forge.

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:11.096
And it's normally laid down--

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:11.931
laying perpendicular.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.499
I've got it standing up.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.835
And so this is the first time
I've used it in this fashion.

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:18.204
I hope it works for me.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.107
I'm going to take my forge
and set up underneath.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.110
That way, I get a normal
heat treat all the way

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:26.212
from the blade tip to the tank.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.681
This heat treat process
is the most critical part.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:31.250
If you don't have the heat
treat process down right,

00:02:31.316 --> 00:02:33.920
then all you have is
a blade-shaped object.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.187
You know, it's not
going to stay sharp.

00:02:35.287 --> 00:02:37.256
So I've got to get
this heat treat done.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.824
It has to happen today.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.359
It's go time.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.262
If it doesn't go right, I don't
know when I'm going to do.

00:02:48.066 --> 00:02:50.803
[sighs] I do have a slight warp.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.545
We're good.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:02.481 line:0%
I'm out of the woods, but
still have some work to do.

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.851 line:0%
 So I was tempering
last night with the torch

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:09.455 line:0%
and screwed the pooch a
little bit and got way too hot

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.489 line:7%
on my blade.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:11.724
So I've lost a lot
of hardness, and I'm

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.225
going to have to re-quench.

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:15.794
I've never done a
torch tempering before,

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.531
and I guess that's what I get
for my lack of experience.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:22.434
A second quench is
just additional risk.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:25.003
Every time you quench, there's
a risk of extra warping,

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.073
of a crack, a broken blade.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.409
It is quite a setback.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.144
If this quench fails,
I may be forced

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:34.480
to start over from scratch.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.215
Here we go.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:39.619
[blowing]

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.221
[blade scraping]

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.323
Definitely hard.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.025
Disaster averted for now so
long as I can get the tempering

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.027
right on my second try.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:51.297
This time around, I'm going to
be really slow, really careful.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.866
And I've got my heat gun right
here pointing at this blade

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.967
the whole time.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.069
If it goes above
350 degrees, I'm

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.537
going to immediately
pull the torch

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:01.274
and make sure that I don't
overtemper this blade again.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.508
The deed is done.

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:05.210
It should be a strong,
hard blade now.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.013
I'm going to move forward,
put a handle on this,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.382
polish it up, turn
it into the judges.

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:14.486
JONATHAN: It's the
start of the last day.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.323
It's raining like cow piss
on a flat rock outside,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.126
so we're working on the
handle and the pommel.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.927
And just a little bit of
clean up and sharpening,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.864
and we're done.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.767
Now I'm going to
go into shaping.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.535
That feels good and
balanced right there.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:32.204
The farther along I got in
this build, the more confident

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:34.206
I became in the weapon.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:35.942
I didn't have enough
time to test it,

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:39.078
but I'm confident
that it'll pass.

00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:42.414
Ladies and gentlemen,
the boar sword.

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.717
 All right, bladesmiths,
to test the lethality

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.986
of your boar swords,
I will deliver thrusts

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:50.756
and cuts on this boar carcass.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:51.424
Jon, you're first.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.124
You ready for this?

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:54.026
 Absolutely.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:58.965
[blade impact sounds]

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:04.937
Yeah.

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.311
All right, Jon, first
up, I like the balance.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:14.080
I like that I can
put two hands on it.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.115
It's void enough to
where I can hold on

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.850
and I can tell
where the edge is.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:21.487
And when we're pushing and
thrusting as it's meant to be,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:25.558
the tip is sharp enough to
thrust all the way through.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:29.562
Your edges, as you can see,
are sharp enough to cut pieces

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.230
out of this boar carcass.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.865
Overall, sir, it'll kill.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:34.900
 Thanks, sir.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:35.901
 Congrats.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.303
 Thanks, man.

00:05:37.369 --> 00:05:38.437
 All right, Isaac, your turn.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:39.304
Are you ready for this?

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:42.775
 Let's make some bacon.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:47.080
[blade impact sounds]

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:49.615
[grunts]

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:58.824
All right, Isaac, first
up, it's much lighter,

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:02.561
so it's easier to control when
you're moving with a blade.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.431
And as you can see, when
I was thrusting in there,

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.600
the point you have here,
the edges are very sharp.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.135
It thrust all the way in.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:12.938
And even when it hits bone,
it's got a very good flex to it.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.507
Did not pick up a bend.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:19.812
Overall, sir, your boar sword
will make the bacon and kill.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:20.980
 Thank you.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.381
 Gentlemen, it's time
for the strength test--

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:24.950
the sheet metal stab.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.019
Now, to test the strength
and overall construction

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:28.888
of your blades, I'll be
stabbing into the sheet metal.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:32.858
But this test is not about what
your blades do to that target.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.927
It's about what that
target does to your blades.

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:35.795
Jonathan, you're first.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:36.328
You ready?

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:37.229
 Absolutely.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:40.767
[blade impact sounds]

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:55.147
 All right Jonathan, your
blade is still sharp pretty

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:56.449
much all the way to the tip.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.750
Now, the tip did get
flattened a little bit,

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:01.821
but that was a very, very acute
tip that you had on there.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.090
All in all, it's a
comfortable weapon.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:06.091
It certainly held
up beautifully.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:06.859
Nicely done.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:07.960
 Thank you.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.196
 All right, Isaac,
are you ready for this?

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:13.866
 As ready as I'm going to be.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:18.204
[blade impact sounds]

00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:28.547
 There is definitely
a significant bend.

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:31.016
 All right, there's a good
flex in your blade, which

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:32.384
we saw in an earlier test.

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:33.786
But when you
quenched this blade,

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:36.155
I'm assuming right
in here somewhere

00:07:36.221 --> 00:07:38.224
was where that quench stopped.

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:41.994
So this is not really
solid right here.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:47.099
You did lose your tip up
here, but your edges held up.

00:07:47.165 --> 00:07:48.434
It's still sharp.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.536
But you can just see
there's an obvious issue

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:51.937
with that bend there.

00:07:52.037 --> 00:07:55.707
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the sharpness test.

00:07:55.807 --> 00:07:57.977
To find out if there's any
sharpness left on your tip

00:07:58.043 --> 00:08:00.379
and edges, I will take
your weapon and stab

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:02.515
and slash at this deer hide.

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:04.016
Now, unlike the
strength test, this

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:07.052
is all about what your blade
will do to this deer hide.

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:07.920
Jon, you're first.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.754
You ready for this?

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:11.456
 Let's do it.

00:08:11.523 --> 00:08:16.028
[blade impact sounds]

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:28.174
 All right, Jon,
looking at the tip here,

00:08:28.241 --> 00:08:29.575
I can see where
it flattened out.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.377
Took a little bit of effort
to be able to puncture

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:33.311
through, but it did.

00:08:33.378 --> 00:08:35.214
Your edges are still sharp.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.682
The cuts are clean.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:39.050
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.252
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:41.319
 All right, Isaac,
your turn, sir.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.154
Are you ready?

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:42.922
 I am.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.896
[blade impact sounds]

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:57.069
 It's about what I expected.

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.336
 I straightened it.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:01.073
 Oh, did you?

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.542
 The damage to your
tip on the strength

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:04.643
test really took it out.

00:09:04.709 --> 00:09:05.610
There is no tip to this anymore.

00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:07.145
I can put my finger on that.

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:11.016
But the edge of your blade on
both sides, as you can see,

00:09:11.116 --> 00:09:12.651
cut all the way through.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.153
Now, the interesting
thing to note

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.155
is that all that
bending actually

00:09:16.255 --> 00:09:18.057
straightened your blade.

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:20.826
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:23.428
 Thank you.

00:09:23.495 --> 00:09:25.564
 Bladesmiths, the
judges have deliberated

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:26.765
right here on the forge floor.

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:28.100
They've made their
final decision.

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:35.040
 Isaac, your blade
didn't make the cut.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.276
Your blade took a bend
in the strength test.

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.744
And for that reason,
I have to ask

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.047
you to please leave the forge.

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:42.948
ISAAC: The end-all
be-all of this task

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.483
was the fact that I couldn't
get a full heat treat

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.286
all the way up
and down my blade,

00:09:47.352 --> 00:09:48.821
and that's what sent me home.

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:51.556
I made it to second place,
and regardless of the results

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.425
of this whole thing, it's
been the best birthday

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.594
present I've ever gotten.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:00.065
 Well, Jonathan, it would
appear the warrior ethos

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:02.567
runs deep in you,
because not only are you

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:03.935
an active duty Marine.

00:10:04.002 --> 00:10:06.739
You are also the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:09.975
That's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:10.976
Congratulations.

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:11.877
[applause]

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:13.212
 Thank you.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:16.549
Being "Forged in Fire"
champion, it feels great.

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:17.382
 Good job.

00:10:17.482 --> 00:10:18.416
 Thank you.

00:10:18.483 --> 00:10:19.684
It's a boost of confidence.

00:10:19.784 --> 00:10:21.086
It's not the big things
that really matter.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.687
It's the little things--
the attention to detail--

00:10:22.754 --> 00:10:24.523
that make a big difference.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:27.093
[dramatic music]

